WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.520
<b>September 21, 2001</b>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.950
<b>Local Time 9:11</b>

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>Commercial District - Lilifort</b>

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.460
Hello.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.130
I bet we'll see the aurora today.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.500
I wonder what color it'll be.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.940
I think it'll be red.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:45.190
<b>The World Bares Its Fangs</b>

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.150
The Raptor's basic combat doctrine

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:23.000
is to use its stealth and supercruise 
for a quick lock and quick kill.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.730
In other words, by the time you see 
it on radar you're already dead.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:33.420
The problem is that it's fast and 
maneuverable, and good at close-range combat.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.710
The Eishi piloting it are 
experts at fighting TSFs.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:42.400
So let's get our strategy conference 
for the Infinities fight started!

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.640
Nobody's got any ideas?

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.490
What about you?

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.940
Well, hmm...

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:57.060
Think of something before you 
start asking other people.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.860
We've just gotta have enough guts to 
dodge them and smack them right back!

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.460
Smack them right back!

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.380
You saw them against the Bao-Feng,

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.080
and Bao-Feng's all about maneuverability.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.000
They got whipped.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.000
Keep howling and people will start 
treating you like a dog, Chihuahua.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.300
I'm not a Chihuahua, I'm Chobi!

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.570
But the more I think about 
it, the tougher they seem.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.010
Looks like you're having a rough time.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.510
If you want,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.020
you can have a practice round with us as the 
aggressors before your fight with the Infinities.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.540
What's she talking about?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:42.130
No, they've already got experience fighting 
TSFs with stealth, it's not a bad idea.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:48.570
If we limit our own sensors we can 
simulate their stealth capability, huh?

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:51.050
I think it's a good offer, but...

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.480
Impossible.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.090
You'll never be able to understand Yuuya.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.250
That's true.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.720
I'll speak to my superiors.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:03.860
Then it's decided.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.520
But I've got a condition.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:07.740
A condition?

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.140
Yuuya Bridges!

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.940
You have to go on a date 
with me all day today!

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.140
A date?

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.760
Cryska?

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.330
Cryska?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.930
Cryska!

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.440
Cryska, where are you?

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.420
Cryska...

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.800
A date...

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.310
It doesn't bother me, really!

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.310
That's right! I am not upset!

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:55.810
Not at all!

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.740
Who's there? Do you want something from me?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.570
Ensign Barchenowa?

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.570
Umm...

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:17.750
Excuse me, I'd like to see Ensign Bridges...

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.750
Yuuya left for Lilifort.

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.010
I see.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.970
You call him "Yuuya", don't you?

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.650
Oh, it's because of Blue Flag.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.240
The schedule for the 
exercises is pretty packed,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.920
so we're running through a lot of supplies.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.220
So we've started using 
civilian suppliers, I heard.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:57.370
Civilians, huh?

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.630
It's almost time.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.630
<b>Yukon Base UN Patrol Standby Hangar</b>

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.620
Calm down a little, kid.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.810
There's no BETA here.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.920
Our enemies here are humans.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:21.650
Well, the warning level's never gone up.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:27.660
The only people here with real bullets 
in their guns are the patrols and us.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:32.370
In other words, if we're not doing anything 
it means the whole world's peaceful.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.860
Why are they so relaxed?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.100
All the peace here has addled their brains!

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.710
How were the North African battle lines?

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.280
Hell.

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:45.600
More starved than died from the BETA.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:50.800
The bureaucrats and the soldiers 
took all the food the UN sent!

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.100
You sound just like the RLF.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.560
The Refugee Liberation Front?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.380
Maybe because my whole family 
died in a refugee camp.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:03.530
I see.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:07.620
Then why didn't you join the RLF?

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.930
Because they're...

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.330
Sorry to bother you when you're on standby, 
but we have maintenance work scheduled.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.160
May we begin?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:22.660
Sure.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:23.780
Thanks.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.460
You-

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:35.140
I'm sorry you didn't get to fight with us.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.330
It's command.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:39.360
Orders. Read them.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.160
That security camera won't 
be a problem, will it?

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.610
The other sleeper agents have 
already taken care of it.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:50.930
Impressive.

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:53.420
His plan is perfect.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:56.500
Camouflage code. Install it.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.080
What about the US and USSR's TSF forces?

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.880
Another unit's taken care of them.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.560
Red nobles? Hah!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.740
You treated us like insects!

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.440
That's right. Show them.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.410
That their days of playing 
at being ruler are over.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:35.700
Boot-up complete.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.170
All 36 TSFs can be launched in slave mode.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.200
Report to HQ.

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:44.530
Synch your launch timing with 
the other attack squads.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:49.120
We shall test those who must be tested 
in accordance with the Lord's plan.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:53.090
Our sacrifice is the only 
way to fix this world.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.300
May the grace of God be with you.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.300
What's wrong, Yuuya? Are you sick?

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.250
Okay, blow.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.070
Good job.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:16.370
You sure you didn't get a weird 
disease from the girl behind you?

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:19.450
What about you? You've 
had all your shots, right?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.280
At the vet?

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:22.240
What?

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.000
You really do bark all the time.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.060
What are you even doing here?

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.680
What about you?

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.060
Tarisa, get that.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.460
This is Argos 2.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:36.970
What's wrong?

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:38.740
Nothing.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:43.970
Ahem. Report in on your 
observation of the date.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.690
Thank you for coming, Lt. Dahl.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.720
So what can I do for you?

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:55.680
Actually, there's been a problem.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.610
A problem? What?

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.490
About Ensign Bridges.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:11.210
Are you aware that Bridges has been 
seen an unusual amount of times

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.840
in the company of our own Ensign Barchenowa?

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.080
Daddy!

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.450
This is the Operator room.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:35.130
Lt. Takamura of the XFJ plan. 
Put me through to Lt. Dahl.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:37.030
A moment.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.570
MPs?

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.010
Did something happen?

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:55.630
Of course, the USSR respects 
the privacy of the individual.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.250
However, they both have 
their positions to consider.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:04.900
The cold war never ended, it was simply 
put on hold by the appearance of the BETA.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:05.650
I see.

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:07.390
Excuse me.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:09.810
Conference room 8.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.060
Yes, it's me.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.360
Lt. Takamura? What's wrong?

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:16.940
<b>Local Time 1500</b>

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.040
I see.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.530
A practice round.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.450
I'll speak to Heinemann-san...

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:31.660
Hello?

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.580
Lt. Dahl?

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.080
Hello?

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:37.300
- Yuuya, there's a spot on your 
clothes. I'll wipe it off.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:37.300
- Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.730
- Hey, get off me!

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:43.340
- This hurricane woman won't 
keep her hands off Yuuya!

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.340
What are they doing?

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:45.600
What?

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.240
Hey. Tarisa?

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.740
Who are you?

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.070
How did you get here?

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.460
How did you know about this lab?

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.890
The only thing you're allowed 
to do is answer the questions.

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:14.690
I'm the one asking them, doctor.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:15.670
What?

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.420
You've got a job to do.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.290
Your evil deeds are going 
to go down in history.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:34.240
Excuse me. We were asked 
to bring these here.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.730
Civilians aren't allowed in here-

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:43.980
Clear.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:43.290
Mommy! Mommy! Mommy! Get up! Mommy!

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.340
Mommy... Mommy...

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:00.650
Someone's attacked the base.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:01.900
Get us out of here.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.540
Hey, are you okay?

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:17.200
What the hell's going on?

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:23.050
Hurry.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:30.080
VG, can you hear me?

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.260
Come on.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.760
What's going on? Is it not working?

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.120
The military comm system is down?

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:37.720
I've got a bad feeling.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:39.600
Yuuya, ahead of us!

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:49.730
What was that?

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.520
The civilians on the rear 
don't know how to act.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:55.740
Wasn't that Natalie?

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.100
What's she doing in a delivery truck?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:14:59.170
Tarisa.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:00.540
What?

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:05.090
Call someone on the emergency 
frequency. It doesn't matter who.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:05.920
Got it.

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:10.590
That's strange. Nobody's picking up.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.590
Hang on tight!

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.680
This happened before.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:21.640
Yeah. At Kamchatka.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:28.120
Commander, it's time.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:32.910
Oh, it's fine to keep the Americans waiting.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.300
Nobody move.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:41.570
Anybody who moves, we'll shoot.

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:43.260
Who are you?

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:44.840
Where are you from?

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:49.160
The enemy's not always on the outside, sir.

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:49.840
You bastard...

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:52.730
Sorry to bother you when you're so busy,

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:56.350
but we'd like you to take us to the 
central planning room, Commander.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.860
I don't know what rebel group you're with,

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.520
but do you really think you're 
going to get away with this?

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.980
We're the RLF, sir.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:10.960
The Refugee Liberation 
Front? What are you after?

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.410
True Freedom and Equality.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:25.060
Are you sure you didn't want to 
drop that kid off at Lilifort?

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.180
The shelters are safer right now.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.650
We don't know what's going to happen there.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:34.050
What the hell is going on?

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.450
Explain!

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:36.740
I don't know.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:39.510
But somebody's trying to 
take over the command...

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:04.480
This is a military action, planned in 
advance and executed with precision.

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.670
We must meet up with our 
units and respond in force.

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.120
Let's split up.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.920
It reduces the risk of 
us both being captured.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:14.840
I pray for your safety.

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:17.590
You too, Lt. Sandek.

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:35.360
I need to get to the hangar 
as soon as possible.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.780
Wait, it's just me.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.810
Ensign Barchenowa?

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.370
What the heck?

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:58.220
Look.

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:00.720
That smoke's coming from the hangar!

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:02.720
Damn it! What the hell's going on?

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.270
Who are they?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.920
Are you two okay?

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.580
I guess so.

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.920
Damn! They just opened fire...

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.350
Don't move.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:50.520
This isn't good.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:54.130
This base is under our control.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:55.560
Resistance is hopeless.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:57.180
Natalie?

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:02.700
You're kidding me, right?

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.700
Why... What are you doing?

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.700
Say something!

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:09.460
Natalie!

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:14.880
You're Asian,

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:18.690
so you should understand what's 
happening to the Eurasian refugees.

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:24.090
The UN, the world is choosing 
what lives it's going to save.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.360
It's abandoning the weak.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:28.500
But...

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:32.730
So we, the RLF, are going to fix the world.

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:38.530
We're going to free our comrades in Eurasia 
and purge those who horde all the wealth!

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:42.490
Please! Join our fight!

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.800
You're the one who said you 
could understand the peace here,

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:48.560
but you couldn't accept it, right!

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:51.210
What are you talking about?

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:56.750
Somebody has to fight for the oppressed 
and those who are discriminated against!

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:10.420
I can't, Natalie.

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:17.700
I swore to my siblings when 
they died that I'd avenge them.

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:21.080
I'm an Eishi.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:25.490
So I don't fight humans.

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.640
Very well then.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:37.000
You can watch our fight in the next world.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.090
Stop, Natalie!

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:40.690
This kind of terrorism isn't going to work!

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.260
I don't know about that.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.930
This base is on the border of 
the US and Russian militaries.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:47.210
Neither of them can take easy action.

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:51.320
We've got the nuclear reactor, and the 
command station, and the communications facilities.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.620
And all the UN, Soviet, and 
American high ranking officials.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.410
That can't be true.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:04.250
Do you really think you can 
change the world like this?

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.240
This doesn't make sense.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.740
She's talking too much.

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:10.680
Of course.

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:14.750
My comrades have taken over the 
US, UN, and USSR fighting forces.

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:20.500
And we're going to destroy all the 
prototypes that cost so much money, too.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:24.880
Isn't it wonderful, Natalie?

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:29.340
Is she trying to tell us all this?

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:32.820
It's only a matter of time 
until we take over the base.

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:36.600
Once the plan's in its final 
stages nobody can do a thing.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:38.600
Final stages?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.560
America's top secret research...

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:58.540
You talk too much.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.880
Natalie!

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.380
What are you doing?

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:21.770
Run!

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:23.730
Natalie...

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:24.980
Natalie!

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:25.820
Run!

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:32.660
Natalie!

00:24:07.010 --> 00:24:09.160
Launch all TSFs.

00:24:09.160 --> 00:24:11.280
I'm heading for the Royal Guard Hanger.

00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:14.450
Inia went for the Terminator alone...

00:24:14.450 --> 00:24:17.300
Cryska, I'm scared! I'm scared!

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:24.270
<b>The Future Tears Open</b>

00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:21.360
Next time on Total Eclipse: 
The Future Tears Open
